==Latin==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|la|cōrs}}

===Etymology===
{{root|la|ine-pro|*ǵʰer-|id=enclose}}
From {{der|la|itc-pro|-}} {{affix|itc-pro|*kom|*horti-|nocat=1}}, the latter a ''ti''-derivative of what is likely the same root underlying {{m|itc-pro|*hortos|t=enclosure}}. {{surf|la|con-|alt1=co-|hortus|alt2=-hors}}.<ref>{{R:itc:EDL|page=123|head=cohors, -tis}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|cohors}}

===Noun===
{{la-noun|cohors<3.I>|g=f}}

# a [[court]]
# a [[farmyard]] or [[enclosure]]
#* {{Q|la|Ovid|Fasti|4|703|thru=704|quote=is capit extrēmī volpem convalle salictī;<br/>abstulerat multās illa '''cohortīs''' avēs.|trans=He catches a vixen in a ravine at the end of a willow grove;<br/>she had carried off many '''farmyard''' birds.}}
# a [[retinue]] or [[escort]]
# a [[circle]] or [[crowd]]
# a [[cohort]]; [[tenth]] part of a [[legion]]
# a [[band]] or [[armed]] [[force]]
# a [[ship]]'s [[crew]]
# a [[bodyguard]]
# a [[military]] unit of 500 men

